    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div>\n<p><em>You walk at the edge where all lies eventually break.</em></p><p>Once per <strong>a Soma Break</strong>, as an <strong>action</strong>, you can open a Truth Horizon for <strong>1 minute</strong>.</p><ul><li>You create a <strong>6 squares-radius aura</strong> that moves with you.</li><li>Within the aura, creatures cannot gain the benefits of <strong>invisibility</strong> or <strong>illusion-based disguise</strong> against you and your allies; their true position and general outline are perceptible.</li><li>Creatures within the aura have <strong>disadvantage</strong> on <strong>Stealth (Intrigue) checks</strong>, and you and your allies have <strong>advantage</strong> on checks to see through lies, illusions, or glamours (usually Insight (Soul) or Investigation (Mind)).</li><li>The first time each creature within the aura attempts to impose roll 3d10 keep lowest 2 on a roll via Stealth, misdirection, or fear-mongering, that disadvantage is<strong>ignored</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Strategic Echo.</strong> If a major investigation, trial, or Spark/Tikkun operation resolved under the Truth Horizon exposes a hidden corruption and leads to a <strong>Justice/Reformation</strong> style outcome instead of Subjugation or Ruin, your faction may gain <strong>+1 Intrigue OP</strong>, <strong>+1 Soft Power OP</strong>, and reduce an appropriate <strong>Darkness Track</strong> by 1.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
